@startuml sequence_logging_pipeline
!theme plain
title Diagnostic Logging Pipeline – configure_logging → handlers → retrieval

' NOTE: This is backend *diagnostic* logging (exceptions, warnings, lifecycle,
' component activation).  For the *experiment-results* pipeline (metrics /
' checkpoints / manifests) see sequence_experiment_logging.puml.

actor Operator as Op
participant "service.run()\n(app process)" as Run
participant "runner.main()\n(subprocess)" as Runner
participant "logging_config\n.configure_logging" as Cfg
participant "root logger\n(+ uvicorn.*, py.warnings)" as Root
participant "StreamHandler\n(stdout)" as Console
participant "RotatingFileHandler\nservice.log" as FileH
participant "FastAPI\n/app.py" as API
participant "Filesystem /\nDocker" as FS

== App process startup ==
Op -> Run: python -m deap_pettingzoo.service [--verbose|--log-level|--log-format]
Run -> Run: resolve_level / resolve_format\nexport DEAP_LOG_LEVEL + DEAP_LOG_FORMAT (env)
note right of Run: env is inherited by the\nrunner subprocess later
Run -> Cfg: configure_logging(log_file=<DEAP_LOG_DIR>/service.log)
Cfg -> Root: dictConfig(level, formatter=plain|json)
Cfg -> Console: attach (stdout)
Cfg -> FileH: attach (rotating, on results volume)
Cfg -> Cfg: logging.captureWarnings(True)
Run -> API: uvicorn.run(..., log_config=None)
note right of API: log_config=None so uvicorn\ndoes not clobber our handlers

== Emission (both processes) ==
API -> Root: logger.info / warning / exception(...)
Runner -> Cfg: configure_logging(log_file=None)  // console only
Runner -> Root: build_configs INFO (components active),\nsub-run progress, logger.exception on failure
group warnings.warn(...)  (parallel / device / coevolution / catalog / rl_side / rl_hpo_side / agilerl_hpo_trainer)
    Root -> Root: routed to py.warnings @ WARNING\n(no stack trace)
end
group Dual-emit pattern (exception sites in RL training code)
    note over Root
      At every except...as exc: block that calls warnings.warn(),
      RL code (rl_side.py, rl_hpo_side.py, agilerl_hpo_trainer.py)
      also calls logger.warning(..., exc_info=True) FIRST so the
      full stack trace lands in service.log, then warnings.warn()
      for the user-visible console message.
      Reference implementation: recording.py:88, agilerl_trainer.py:926.
    end note
end
Root -> Console: format + write
Root -> FileH: format + write (app process only)

note over Console,FileH
  Level gate (the --verbose switch):
    WARNING  (default) = warnings + exceptions only
    INFO     (-v)      = + lifecycle + components active
    DEBUG    (-vv)     = + hyperparameters / requests
end note

== Retrieval ==
Console -> FS: app stdout  -> docker compose logs service
FileH   -> FS: service.log -> docker exec/cp, volume
Runner  -> FS: runner stdout -> <exp_dir>/_stdout.log
Op -> API: GET /logs?lines=N           -> tail service.log
Op -> API: GET /experiments/{id}/stdout -> tail _stdout.log

@enduml
